      "excerpts": [
        "The World War and subsequent events changed the United States from the world's greatest debtor to that of the second greatest creditor.",
        "We think and act like debtors; our policies are those that suited the pre-war period.\\nThis change in our international financial position vitally affects the export farmer.",
        "Table III, which gives the change in our debtor-creditor position, demands serious study.",
        "The story it tells is so important to the well-being of Iowa.",
        "farm people that it would be well if this table were framed and hung in every farm home in the state."
      ]
